<title>USA: April Brent ends mixed in late U.S. trading.</title>
<headline>April Brent ends mixed in late U.S. trading.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-02-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>North Sea Brent ended mixed in late U.S. trading Monday, with a moderate series of partials changing hands, traders said.</p>
<p>Partial April Brent cargoes traded at $20.70-80 a barrel, compared to the IPE settlement price of $20.75.</p>
<p>Traders attributed a major European company with most of the selling.</p>
<p>March/April Brent was dealt at 35 cents and 37 cents, on either side of the London close of 36 cents.</p>
<p>--Patricia Garip-Bertuol NY Energy Desk ((+1 212 859 1620))</p>
